      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A burning sensation in the chest that worsens with physical activity but resolves with rest could indicate heartburn, yet it can also be a symptom of angina or other cardiac issues. Because chest pain during exertion is a classic sign of the heart struggling to meet increased oxygen demand, you should not self-diagnose or simply treat it with antacids without ruling out a serious heart condition immediately. Please stop any physical activity and contact a healthcare provider or emergency service right away for a proper evaluation.",
